      \field{abstract}{We give an introduction to the ideas behind G. S. Tseytin’s 1958 construction of a seven-relation semigroup with undecidable word problem. We give a history of the ideas leading up to its construction, some intuition for the proof, and provide an overview of some subsequent results and developments which stem from this remarkable semigroup. An English translation of Tseytin’s article [73] by the author of the present article is supplemented at the end of the article (the Russian original was published in Trudy Mat. Inst. Steklov 52 (1958), pp. 172–189).}
